IMPORT prelude

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Western Australia) -- the first home buyer: do I qualify for the grant, how much is it,
-- when must I apply, and when must I pay it back.
--
-- SEAT: the first home buyer -- the applicant for a first home owner grant (s 15), who is, or will be on completion, an
-- owner of the home (s 16). Every exported question is phrased as that buyer would ask it. Where the Act addresses only the
-- Commissioner of State Revenue (ss 18, 21, 51, 55), what is encoded is what may be done to the buyer, and by when.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 (transaction, new home, established home, de facto partner, residential property); s 7 (spouse);
-- s 7B (permanent resident); s 8 (entitlement); Part 2 Division 2, ss 9, 9A, 10, 11, 12, 13, 13A, 13B (the eligibility
-- criteria); s 14(1), (3), (5A) (eligible transaction); s 14AA (commencement date); ss 14AB, 14AC (consideration, total
-- value); s 14AD with the Regulations r 6 (cap amount); s 15(5) (when to apply); s 16 (all owners must apply); s 18(2), (3),
-- (5)-(7) (payment before completion and repayment if the cap is exceeded); s 19 (amount of the grant, including the s 19(2)
-- relevant amounts for special eligible transactions, as a table); s 21 (payment in anticipation of residence, and
-- repayment); s 22(4) and s 47 (offences); ss 28 and 31 (objection and review deadlines); s 51 (repayment and penalty);
-- s 52 with the Regulations r 8(3) (interest under a repayment arrangement); s 55 (charge on the home). Also the Duties Act
-- 2008 s 142A test of a "concessional first home owner", which borrows this Act, so that the two baselines agree.
--
-- Edition: compilation of the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Act No. 16 of 2000) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49121.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49121, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit
-- states no compilation number or date; its compilation table ends with the Help to Buy (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2025
-- Pt. 4 Div. 2 (in operation 19 Dec 2025). Regulations: First Home Owner Grant Regulations 2000, version 03-l0-00, currency
-- from 14 May 2026, as deposited at ../../../first-home-owner-grant-regulations-2000/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49370.txt
-- (mrdoc 49370, retrieved 2026-10-20): r 6 (cap amount $800 000 south of the 26th parallel, for transactions commencing on
-- or after 7 May 2026) and r 8(3) (12.4% a year). The dates of "amendment day" (25 Sep 2013) and "second amendment day"
-- (3 Oct 2015) in s 19(1) and s 14(5A) are read from the Act's compilation table (Revenue Laws Amendment Act 2013 Pt. 4;
-- Revenue Laws Amendment Act 2015 Pt. 2 Div. 1).
--
-- Dates are entered as YYYYMMDD numbers (7 May 2026 is 20260507), so that date tests are simple comparisons.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the s 14B tests of which special class a transaction falls in (the windows all closed by 30 June 2017; the
-- class is a FACT here, and only its s 19(2) amount is encoded); the s 14(5) owner-builder cap exemption before 2009;
-- movable buildings (s 14AA(3)); the relevant interest prescribed by regulations rr 4 and 5 and the s 16 exclusions in r 7
-- (whether every owner who must apply has applied is one FACT); applications by a guardian (s 17) and death of an applicant
-- (s 23); the Commissioner's power to correct a decision (s 24) beyond its effect through s 51; the objection procedure
-- (ss 29-30A, 32); the investigation powers (Part 4); the charge's priority, release and sale (ss 56-59); grant relief
-- declarations (Part 6A); administration, confidentiality and regulations.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the first home buyer, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 -- the first home buyer`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 3 -- the transaction`

-- s 3: "transaction means -- (a) a contract for the purchase of a home in the State; or (b) a comprehensive home building
-- contract made by the owner of land in the State, or a person who will on completion of the contract be the owner of land
-- in the State, to have a home built on the land; or (c) the building of a home in the State by an owner builder".
-- "new home means a home that has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence"; a "substantially renovated
-- home" is one sold as new residential premises under the GST Act and not since occupied or sold; "established home means a
-- home that is not a new home or a substantially renovated home". Which of these a home is, is a FACT the buyer states.
DECLARE `Kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a contract to buy a new home`
    `a contract to buy a substantially renovated home`
    `a contract to buy an established home`
    `a comprehensive home building contract`
    `building a home as an owner builder`

-- s 14AD: "(a) in relation to a home south of the 26th parallel of South Latitude ...; or (b) in relation to a home north of
-- the 26th parallel of South Latitude". Perth and the south-west are south of it; which side a home is on is a FACT.
DECLARE `Side of the 26th parallel` IS ONE OF
    `south of the 26th parallel`
    `north of the 26th parallel`

-- s 14A and s 14B: special eligible transactions, classes 1 to 8, each tied to a commencement-date window that closed by
-- 30 June 2017. The class is a FACT here.
DECLARE `Special class` IS ONE OF
    `not a special eligible transaction`
    `class 1`
    `class 2`
    `class 3`
    `class 4`
    `class 5`
    `class 6`
    `class 7`
    `class 8`

-- One case is one transaction (s 8(3): "Only one first home owner grant is payable for the same eligible transaction").
-- `commencement date`: s 14AA(1): for a contract, "the date when the contract is made"; for an owner builder, the date
-- "laying the foundations for the home begins" (or another date the Commissioner considers appropriate).
-- `completion date`: s 14AA(2): a purchase is completed when "the purchaser acquires the relevant interest in land"; a
-- building contract or owner build when "the building is ready for occupation as a place of residence". 0 if not yet.
-- `consideration`: s 14AB: the price; the "total consideration payable for the building work"; or the owner builder's
-- "actual costs ... excluding any allowance for the owner builder's own labour".
-- `unencumbered value of the home`: s 14AE: its value disregarding encumbrances and non-arm's-length or value-reducing
-- arrangements -- for a purchase, of the property at the commencement date; for an owner build, of the home at completion.
DECLARE Transaction HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of transaction`
    `commencement date` IS A NUMBER
    `completion date` IS A NUMBER
    `where the home is` IS A `Side of the 26th parallel`
    `consideration` IS A NUMBER
    `unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER
    `consideration paid for the land` IS A NUMBER
    `unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER
    `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner has declared it eligible under s 14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied it replaced a contract made before amendment day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special class` IS A `Special class`

§§ `ss 3, 7, 11 and 12 -- the applicant, the applicant's partner, and their history`

-- The history of a person, as ss 11 and 12 ask it.
-- s 11(1): "has been a party to another application under this Act or a corresponding law; and (b) a first home owner grant
-- (the other grant) has been paid on the other application."
-- s 12(1): "has, before 1 July 2000, held -- (a) a relevant interest in residential property in the State, other than a
-- relevant interest held subject to a trust; or (b) an interest in residential property in another State or a Territory that
-- is a relevant interest under the corresponding law". s 12(3): before the commencement date, held such an interest "and
-- (b) occupied the property as a place of residence -- (i) before 1 July 2004; or (ii) for a continuous period of at least
-- 6 months that began on or after 1 July 2004."
-- s 3(2): land is "residential property" if there is on it "a building ... lawfully occupied as a place of residence or
-- suitable for occupation as a place of residence". s 6: a "relevant interest" is chiefly a fee simple, a strata lease, or a
-- Crown lease or purchase that leads to one. Whether a person held one is asked as a FACT.
DECLARE History HAS
    `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
    `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` IS A NUMBER

-- s 7(1): a person is the applicant's spouse if "on the commencement date ... the person is married to the applicant";
-- s 7(2): not so if the Commissioner is satisfied they are "living apart" with "no intention of again living together as a
-- couple". s 3: "de facto partner ... means a person who, on the commencement date ..., is living in a de facto relationship
-- with the applicant and has lived on that basis with the applicant for at least 2 years".
-- Each person who is, or might be, the applicant's spouse or de facto partner is listed with these facts.
DECLARE Partner HAS
    `is married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with me in a de facto relationship on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years we have lived together on that basis` IS A NUMBER
    `their history` IS A History

-- s 7B(1): a permanent resident is "(a) ... (i) the holder of a permanent visa ...; or (ii) a New Zealand citizen who is the
-- holder of a special category visa ...; and (b) the person has satisfied the Commissioner that he or she intends to reside
-- permanently in Australia". Citizenship and the visas are the Commonwealth Acts' terms, asked as FACTS.
-- `months after completion before I begin living in the home` and `continuous months I live in the home` describe the
-- residence the buyer has kept, or intends to keep (s 13).
-- `residence months approved by the Commissioner` and `takeup months approved by the Commissioner` are 0 unless the
-- Commissioner has approved a shorter residence period or a longer takeup period under s 13(6A).
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has satisfied the Commissioner I intend to reside permanently in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my history` IS A History
    `my partners` IS A LIST OF Partner
    `the other grant was paid back under its conditions, with any penalty and interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I notified the residence breach, it was paid back, and the Commissioner thinks I should not be ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been convicted of an offence under this Act or a corresponding law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `will hold the relevant interest as a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only part held as trustee is under a Help to Buy arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months after completion before I begin living in the home` IS A NUMBER
    `continuous months I live in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A NUMBER
    `residence months approved by the Commissioner` IS A NUMBER
    `takeup months approved by the Commissioner` IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner has exempted me from the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 16(1): "All interested persons must be applicants, unless such a person is excluded ... by the regulations"; an
-- interested person is one who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home. Regulation 7 excludes, for example, a
-- guarantor co-owner required by a lender (r 7(2D)). Whether every owner who must apply has applied is one FACT.
DECLARE Application HAS
    `applicants` IS A LIST OF Applicant
    `the transaction` IS A Transaction
    `every owner who must apply has applied` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `ss 3 and 7 -- who is my spouse or de facto partner`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is my spouse or de facto partner` IF
        (    `the person`'s `is married to me on the commencement date`
         AND (NOT (`the person`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied we live apart for good`)))
    OR  (    `the person`'s `lives with me in a de facto relationship on the commencement date`
         AND `the person`'s `years we have lived together on that basis` AT LEAST 2)

@export Is this person my spouse or de facto partner for the first home owner grant (ss 3 and 7)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A Partner @desc The person, and how you live together on the commencement date of the transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my spouse or de facto partner` IF `is my spouse or de facto partner` `the person`

-- The histories that count against an applicant: their own, and each spouse's or de facto partner's.
GIVEN `partners` IS A LIST OF Partner
GIVETH A LIST OF History
`the histories of the spouses and partners in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `partners`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `p` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `is my spouse or de facto partner` `p`
        THEN `p`'s `their history` FOLLOWED BY `the histories of the spouses and partners in` `rest`
        ELSE `the histories of the spouses and partners in` `rest`

GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A LIST OF History
`the histories that count for` MEANS
    `me`'s `my history` FOLLOWED BY `the histories of the spouses and partners in` (`me`'s `my partners`)

GIVEN `histories` IS A LIST OF History
      `test` IS A FUNCTION FROM History TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some history` MEANS
    CONSIDER `histories`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `h` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN `test` `h` OR `some history` `rest` `test`

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- the eligibility criteria`

-- s 9: "An applicant for a first home owner grant must be a natural person."
-- s 9A(1): "must be at least 18 years of age"; (2): the Commissioner "may exempt" an applicant if satisfied the applicant
-- intends to meet the residence requirements and the application is not "part of a scheme to circumvent" the limits. The
-- exemption is asked as a FACT: the answer holds if the Commissioner has granted it.
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criteria 1 and 1A` IF
        `me`'s `is a natural person`
    AND (`me`'s `age` AT LEAST 18 OR `me`'s `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement`)

@export Am I old enough for the first home owner grant (s 9A)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough` IF `I meet criteria 1 and 1A` `me`

-- s 7B: permanent resident.
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a permanent resident` IF
        (`me`'s `holds a permanent visa` OR `me`'s `is a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa`)
    AND `me`'s `has satisfied the Commissioner I intend to reside permanently in Australia`

GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a citizen or permanent resident` IF
    `me`'s `is an Australian citizen` OR `I am a permanent resident` `me`

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some applicant is a citizen or permanent resident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `applicants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        `I am a citizen or permanent resident` `a` OR `some applicant is a citizen or permanent resident` `rest`

-- s 10(1): "an applicant ... must be an Australian citizen or a permanent resident"; (2): "If an application is made by
-- joint applicants and one of the applicants is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident, it is not necessary for any
-- other to be". Read together: the criterion is met for every applicant if at least one applicant is.
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
      `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criterion 2` IF
    `I am a citizen or permanent resident` `me`
    OR `some applicant is a citizen or permanent resident` (`the application`'s `applicants`)

@export Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion (ss 7B and 10)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc The application, with every applicant on it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` IF `I meet criterion 2` `me` `the application`

-- s 11(1): ineligible if the applicant or the applicant's spouse or de facto partner was a party to another application on
-- which a grant was paid. (2) Not ineligible "(a) if the other grant was paid back under the conditions on which it was
-- made; or (b) if" a residence breach was notified, the grant was paid back and "in the Commissioner's opinion, the
-- circumstances do not warrant the applicant's being rendered ineligible." (3) Not paid back unless "any penalty or
-- interest" has also been paid. The Commissioner's opinion is asked as a FACT.
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criterion 3` IF
        (NOT (`some history` (`the histories that count for` `me`) (GIVEN h YIELD h's `was a party to another application on which a grant was paid`)))
    OR  `me`'s `the other grant was paid back under its conditions, with any penalty and interest`
    OR  `me`'s `I notified the residence breach, it was paid back, and the Commissioner thinks I should not be ineligible`

@export Am I free of the bar on a second grant (s 11)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with your history and any spouse or de facto partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I free of the second grant bar` IF `I meet criterion 3` `me`

-- s 12: the prior-ownership test.
GIVEN `h` IS A History
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the history shows a prior home` IF
        `h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`
    OR  (    `h`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date`
         AND (    `h`'s `occupied that property as a residence before 1 July 2004`
              OR  `h`'s `longest continuous months occupying that property from 1 July 2004` AT LEAST 6))

GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criterion 4` IF
    NOT (`some history` (`the histories that count for` `me`) `the history shows a prior home`)

@export Am I a first home owner -- have neither I nor my spouse or de facto partner held a home that counts (s 12)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with your history and any spouse or de facto partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I never owned a home that counts` IF `I meet criterion 4` `me`

-- s 13(1): "must occupy the home as the applicant's principal place of residence for the required residence period";
-- (2): "a continuous period of at least 6 months" or a shorter period approved under (6A)(a); (4): must "begin the required
-- residence period within the takeup period"; (5): "the period of 12 months after completion" or a longer period approved
-- under (6A)(b). Approvals are asked as FACTS (0 = none).
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my required residence months` MEANS
    IF `me`'s `residence months approved by the Commissioner` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `me`'s `residence months approved by the Commissioner`
    ELSE 6

GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my takeup months` MEANS
    IF `me`'s `takeup months approved by the Commissioner` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `me`'s `takeup months approved by the Commissioner`
    ELSE 12

GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I keep the residence requirements myself` IF
        `me`'s `months after completion before I begin living in the home` AT MOST `my takeup months` `me`
    AND `me`'s `continuous months I live in the home as my principal place of residence` AT LEAST `my required residence months` `me`

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF Applicant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number keeping the residence requirements in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `applicants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        (IF `I keep the residence requirements myself` `a` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number keeping the residence requirements in` `rest`

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF Applicant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of applicants in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `applicants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN 1 PLUS `the number of applicants in` `rest`

-- s 13(6): the Commissioner "may exempt an applicant from the residence requirements if -- (a) the applicant is one of 2 or
-- more joint applicants ...; and (b) at least one of the applicants complies with the residence requirements; and (c) there
-- are, in the Commissioner's opinion, good reasons". The exemption (c) is a FACT; (a) and (b) are worked out.
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
      `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criterion 5` IF
        `I keep the residence requirements myself` `me`
    OR  (    `me`'s `the Commissioner has exempted me from the residence requirements`
         AND `the number of applicants in` (`the application`'s `applicants`) AT LEAST 2
         AND `the number keeping the residence requirements in` (`the application`'s `applicants`) AT LEAST 1)

@export Do I meet the residence requirements -- moving in within the takeup period and living there long enough (s 13)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with when you moved in and how long you lived there
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc The application, with every applicant on it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the residence requirements` IF `I meet criterion 5` `me` `the application`

@export How many months must I live in the home as my principal place of residence (s 13(2))?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with any shorter period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months must I live in the home` IS `my required residence months` `me`

@export Within how many months after completion must I move in (s 13(5))?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with any longer period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many months after completion must I move in` IS `my takeup months` `me`

-- s 13A: "An applicant is ineligible if the applicant has been convicted of an offence under this Act or a corresponding law."
-- s 13B(1): ineligible if the applicant will own the home "in circumstances where the applicant holds the relevant interest
-- as a trustee"; (2) not if the only part so held is "as a trustee for the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to
-- Buy arrangement".
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet criteria 6 and 7` IF
        (NOT (`me`'s `has been convicted of an offence under this Act or a corresponding law`))
    AND (    (NOT (`me`'s `will hold the relevant interest as a trustee`))
         OR  `me`'s `the only part held as trustee is under a Help to Buy arrangement`)

-- s 8(1)(a): the applicant "complies with the eligibility criteria" (with the exemptions in s 8(2), folded in above).
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant
      `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet every criterion` IF
        `I meet criteria 1 and 1A` `me`
    AND `I meet criterion 2` `me` `the application`
    AND `I meet criterion 3` `me`
    AND `I meet criterion 4` `me`
    AND `I meet criterion 5` `me` `the application`
    AND `I meet criteria 6 and 7` `me`

@export Am I eligible for the first home owner grant -- do I meet every criterion in Part 2 Division 2 (ss 9 to 13B)?
GIVEN `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc The application, with every applicant on it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible` IF `I meet every criterion` `me` `the application`

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
      `applicants` IS A LIST OF Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every applicant in the list meets every criterion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `applicants`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        `I meet every criterion` `a` `the application`
        AND `every applicant in the list meets every criterion` `the application` `rest`

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every applicant meets every criterion` IF
        `the number of applicants in` (`the application`'s `applicants`) AT LEAST 1
    AND `every applicant in the list meets every criterion` `the application` (`the application`'s `applicants`)

§§ `ss 14 to 14AE and Regulations r 6 -- the eligible transaction and the cap`

-- s 14AD: "(a) in relation to a home south of the 26th parallel of South Latitude, $750 000; or (b) in relation to a home
-- north of the 26th parallel of South Latitude, $1 000 000, except that the regulations may prescribe another amount".
-- Regulations r 6: "(1) The cap amount for the purposes of section 14AD(a) of the Act is $800 000. (2) Subregulation (1)
-- applies in relation to a transaction the commencement date of which is on or after 7 May 2026."
-- s 14(1)(b): the cap that applies "(i) in the case of a contract -- on the commencement date; or (ii) in the case of the
-- building of a home by an owner builder -- on the date the transaction is completed."
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date the cap is fixed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `kind`
    WHEN `building a home as an owner builder` THEN `the transaction`'s `completion date`
    OTHERWISE `the transaction`'s `commencement date`

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap amount for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `where the home is`
    WHEN `north of the 26th parallel` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `south of the 26th parallel` THEN
        IF `the date the cap is fixed` `the transaction` AT LEAST 20260507 THEN 800000 ELSE 750000

@export What is the cap amount -- the highest total value my home can have and still attract the grant (s 14AD; Regulations r 6)?
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the cap amount for my home` IS `the cap amount for` `the transaction`

-- s 14AC(1): total value is "(a) in the case of a contract for the purchase of a home, the greater of -- (i) the
-- consideration ...; and (ii) the unencumbered value, at the commencement date, of the property"; "(b) in the case of a
-- comprehensive home building contract, ... the consideration ...; and (ii) the value, at the commencement date, of the
-- relevant interest in the land"; "(c) in the case of the building of a home by an owner builder, ... (i) the unencumbered
-- value, at the date the transaction is completed, of the home; and (ii) the value ... of the relevant interest in the
-- land". (2): the land's value is "the greater of -- (a) the consideration paid for the interest; and (b) the unencumbered
-- value of the interest."
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the land` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`the transaction`'s `consideration paid for the land`) (`the transaction`'s `unencumbered value of the land`)

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total value of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a comprehensive home building contract` THEN
        `the transaction`'s `consideration` PLUS `the value of the land` `the transaction`
    WHEN `building a home as an owner builder` THEN
        `the transaction`'s `unencumbered value of the home` PLUS `the value of the land` `the transaction`
    OTHERWISE
        `the greater of` (`the transaction`'s `consideration`) (`the transaction`'s `unencumbered value of the home`)

@export What is the total value of my transaction, which is tested against the cap (s 14AC)?
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the total value of my transaction` IS `the total value of` `the transaction`

-- s 14(1): an eligible transaction is one "(a) with a commencement date on or after 1 July 2000; and (b) that has a total
-- value that is less than or equal to any cap amount that applies". (3), (4): a contract under an option or right granted
-- before 1 July 2000 is not eligible unless the Commissioner declares it eligible. (5A): "A contract is not an eligible
-- transaction if -- (a) it is for the purchase of an established home; and (b) it has a commencement date on or after"
-- second amendment day (3 Oct 2015, from the compilation table).
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an eligible transaction but for s 14(5A)` IF
        `the transaction`'s `commencement date` AT LEAST 20000701
    AND `the total value of` `the transaction` AT MOST `the cap amount for` `the transaction`
    AND (    (NOT (`the transaction`'s `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies`))
         OR  `the transaction`'s `the Commissioner has declared it eligible under s 14(4)`)

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is caught by s 14(5A)` IF
        `the transaction`'s `commencement date` AT LEAST 20151003
    AND CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `kind`
        WHEN `a contract to buy an established home` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an eligible transaction` IF
        `it is an eligible transaction but for s 14(5A)` `the transaction`
    AND (NOT (`it is caught by s 14(5A)` `the transaction`))

@export Is my purchase or building contract an eligible transaction (s 14)?
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my transaction eligible` IF `it is an eligible transaction` `the transaction`

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it has been completed` IF `the transaction`'s `completion date` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `s 8 -- is the grant payable`

-- s 8(1): "A first home owner grant is payable on an application under this Act if -- (a) the applicant or, if there are 2
-- or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the eligibility criteria; and (b) the transaction ... (i) is an
-- eligible transaction; and (ii) has been completed." s 16(1): all interested persons must be applicants.
GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is payable` IF
        `every applicant meets every criterion` `the application`
    AND `it is an eligible transaction` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)
    AND `it has been completed` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)
    AND `the application`'s `every owner who must apply has applied`

@export Is the first home owner grant payable on my application (s 8)?
GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant, and the transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the grant payable to me` IF `the grant is payable` `the application`

§§ `s 19 -- the amount of the grant, as a table`

-- s 19(1): "amendment day" is when the Revenue Laws Amendment Act 2013 s 43 came into operation, and "second amendment day"
-- when the Revenue Laws Amendment Act 2015 Part 2 Division 1 did. The compilation table gives 25 Sep 2013 (2013 Act Pt. 4)
-- and 3 Oct 2015 (2015 Act Pt. 2 Div. 1).
-- (2A) before amendment day: the lesser of "$7 000" and "the consideration for the transaction".
-- (2B) from amendment day to second amendment day: "(a) ... an established home, the lesser of ... $3 000 ... (b) ... any
-- other transaction, the lesser of ... $10 000" and the consideration.
-- (2CA) on or after second amendment day: the lesser of "$10 000" and the consideration.
-- (2C) (2A) applies after amendment day if the Commissioner is satisfied the transaction replaced a contract made before it.
DECLARE `Grant period` HAS
    `from` IS A NUMBER
    `established home amount` IS A NUMBER
    `other amount` IS A NUMBER

-- Highest period first: the first row whose `from` the commencement date reaches applies.
`the grant periods` MEANS
    LIST `Grant period` OF 20151003, 10000, 10000
         `Grant period` OF 20130925, 3000, 10000
         `Grant period` OF 20000701, 7000, 7000

GIVEN `periods` IS A LIST OF `Grant period`
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard amount from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `periods`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `p` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the transaction`'s `commencement date` AT LEAST `p`'s `from`
        THEN CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `kind`
             WHEN `a contract to buy an established home` THEN `p`'s `established home amount`
             OTHERWISE `p`'s `other amount`
        ELSE `the standard amount from` `rest` `the transaction`

-- s 19(3): "relevant amount means -- (a) ... class 1 or class 2 ... $14 000; (b) ... class 3 ... $10 000; (c) ... class 4 ...
-- $14 000; (d) ... class 5 ... $21 000; (e) ... class 6 ... $10 500; (f) ... class 7 ... $14 000; (g) ... class 8 ...
-- $15 000."
GIVEN `the class` IS A `Special class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant amount for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `class 1` THEN 14000
    WHEN `class 2` THEN 14000
    WHEN `class 3` THEN 10000
    WHEN `class 4` THEN 14000
    WHEN `class 5` THEN 21000
    WHEN `class 6` THEN 10500
    WHEN `class 7` THEN 14000
    WHEN `class 8` THEN 15000
    WHEN `not a special eligible transaction` THEN 0

-- s 19(2): "Despite anything else in this section, the amount ... for ... a special eligible transaction ... is the lesser
-- of -- (a) the consideration ...; (b) the relevant amount."
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the grant for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction`'s `special class`
    WHEN `not a special eligible transaction` THEN
        IF `the transaction`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied it replaced a contract made before amendment day`
           AND `the transaction`'s `commencement date` AT LEAST 20130925
        THEN `the lesser of` 7000 (`the transaction`'s `consideration`)
        ELSE `the lesser of` (`the standard amount from` `the grant periods` `the transaction`) (`the transaction`'s `consideration`)
    OTHERWISE
        `the lesser of` (`the transaction`'s `consideration`) (`the relevant amount for` (`the transaction`'s `special class`))

@export How much is my first home owner grant, if it is payable (s 19)?
GIVEN `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your eligible transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my grant` IS `the amount of the grant for` `the transaction`

@export How much first home owner grant will I actually be paid on my application (ss 8 and 19)?
GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant, and the transaction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much grant will I be paid` IS
    IF `the grant is payable` `the application`
    THEN `the amount of the grant for` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 15(5) -- when to apply`

-- s 15(5): "The application may only be made within a period -- (a) beginning on the commencement date of the transaction
-- ...; and (b) ending 12 months after the completion of the transaction". (6): the Commissioner may allow it earlier.
@export Up to how many months after completion may I apply for the grant (s 15(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Up to how many months after completion may I apply` IS 12

GIVEN `months after completion` IS A NUMBER
      `applied before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner allowed an early application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is in time` IF
        `months after completion` AT MOST 12
    AND ((NOT `applied before the commencement date`) OR `the Commissioner allowed an early application`)

@export Is my application in time (s 15(5), (6))?
GIVEN `months after completion` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion you apply (0 or less if before completion)
      `applied before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied before the contract was made or the foundations began
      `the Commissioner allowed an early application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner allowed you to apply early
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application in time` IF
    `the application is in time` `months after completion` `applied before the commencement date` `the Commissioner allowed an early application`

§§ `ss 18, 21, 51, 52 and 55 -- when I must pay it back`

-- s 18(2): the Commissioner may pay before completion. (3): if the applicant "becomes aware that the total value of the
-- transaction exceeds, or will exceed, the cap amount", the applicant "must within 30 days ... (a) give written notice ...;
-- and (b) either repay the amount of the grant, or make an application under section 52(2)" for a repayment arrangement.
GIVEN `paid before completion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must notify and repay because the cap is exceeded` IF
    `paid before completion` AND `the total value of` `the transaction` GREATER THAN `the cap amount for` `the transaction`

@export Was I paid early and must I now give notice and repay because the total value is over the cap (s 18(3))?
GIVEN `paid before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before the transaction was completed
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your transaction as it now stands
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay because my home is over the cap` IF
    `I must notify and repay because the cap is exceeded` `paid before completion` `the transaction`

-- s 21(1): the Commissioner may pay "in anticipation of compliance with the residence requirements". (2): if the applicant
-- does not, or becomes aware they will not, begin living there within the takeup period or stay for the residence period,
-- "the applicant must within 30 days after the relevant day -- (d) give written notice ...; and (e) either repay the amount
-- of the grant, or make an application under section 52(2)".
GIVEN `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `me` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must notify and repay because of residence` IF
    `paid in anticipation of residence` AND (NOT (`I keep the residence requirements myself` `me`))

@export Must I give notice and repay the grant because I did not move in or stay long enough (s 21(2))?
GIVEN `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before you had lived in the home for the required period
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You, with when you moved in and how long you lived there
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay because of residence` IF
    `I must notify and repay because of residence` `paid in anticipation of residence` `me`

@export Within how many days must I give notice and repay, or apply for an arrangement, under s 18(3) or s 21(2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I notify and repay` IS 30

-- s 51(1): the Commissioner "may, by written notice, require an applicant ... to repay an amount" if "(a) the amount was paid
-- in error; or (b) the Commissioner reverses the decision ...; or (c) ... a condition ... with which the applicant ... has
-- failed to comply". (4): it "must be paid by the applicant within 28 days after the date on which notice ... is given".
-- ss 18(7), 21(6): a penalty must likewise be paid within 28 days of notice.
GIVEN `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner reversed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I can be required to repay under s 51` IF
    `paid in error` OR `the Commissioner reversed the decision` OR `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time`

@export Can the Commissioner make me repay the grant (s 51(1))?
GIVEN `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid in error
      `the Commissioner reversed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reversed the decision to pay
      `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to meet a condition of the grant within its period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to repay` IF
    `I can be required to repay under s 51` `paid in error` `the Commissioner reversed the decision` `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time`

@export Within how many days of the notice must I pay a required repayment or penalty (s 51(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days of notice must I repay` IS 28

-- ss 18(6), 21(5a), 51(2) and (3): a penalty is "not to exceed" or "not more than" the amount the applicant is required to
-- repay. s 51(5): penalties under (2) and (3) are not cumulative beyond the payment made.
@export What is the most penalty I can be charged on top of the amount I must repay (ss 18(6), 21(5a), 51(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the amount I must repay` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of grant you are required to repay, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most penalty I can be charged` IS `the amount I must repay`

-- s 52(1), (3)(a): the Commissioner may approve an arrangement to pay later or by instalments, with interest "at the
-- prescribed rate". Regulations r 8(3): "The rate of interest for the purposes of section 52(3)(a) and (7) of the Act is 12.4%
-- per annum."
@export What interest rate, per cent a year, is prescribed for a repayment arrangement (s 52(3)(a); Regulations r 8(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What interest rate applies to my repayment arrangement` IS 12.4

-- s 55(1): the Commissioner may lodge a memorial, creating a charge on the home, if the applicant "(a) is liable to pay an
-- amount to which section 53 applies; and (b) holds a relevant interest in relation to the home". (2A): also if the grant was
-- paid under s 21, the applicant holds the interest, and "the Commissioner reasonably believes that the applicant intends to
-- sell the home before the applicant has complied with the residence requirements". The belief is asked as a FACT.
GIVEN `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I still own the home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a charge can be put on my home` IF
        `I still own the home`
    AND (    `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs`
         OR  (`paid in anticipation of residence` AND `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements`))

@export Can the Commissioner register a charge over my home for the grant (s 55)?
GIVEN `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe a repayment, penalty, arrangement amount or costs under the Act
      `I still own the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you still hold the relevant interest in the home
      `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid before you met the residence requirements
      `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reasonably believes you intend to sell before meeting them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a charge be put on my home` IF
    `a charge can be put on my home` `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs` `I still own the home` `paid in anticipation of residence` `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements`

§§ `ss 22, 47, 28 and 31 -- offences, objection and review`

-- s 22(4): "A person who fails to comply with a condition imposed by the Commissioner ... commits an offence. Penalty: $20 000."
-- s 47(1): providing information or a document "that is false or misleading in a material particular" -- "Penalty: $20 000",
-- with a defence (2) of not knowing and not being reckless. A conviction also makes the person ineligible for any later grant
-- (s 13A).
@export What is the most I can be fined for giving false or misleading information, or breaking a grant condition (ss 22(4), 47)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined` IS 20000

-- s 28(1)(a): an objection "is to be lodged -- (a) within 60 days after the date on which notice of the decision is given";
-- (2), (3): the Commissioner may extend, on an application made "within 12 months after the day on which the objection was to
-- have been lodged". s 31(2): an application to the State Administrative Tribunal "is to be made within 60 days after the
-- date on which notice of the decision is given".
@export Within how many days of notice of the decision must I object (s 28(1)(a))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I object` IS 60

@export Within how many days of the objection decision must I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal (s 31(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I seek review` IS 60

§§ `Duties Act 2008 s 142A -- am I a concessional first home owner for transfer duty`

-- Duties Act 2008 s 142A(1): a concessional first home owner is "(a) a transferee who is paid a first home owner grant ... or
-- to whom a first home owner grant is or will be payable ...; or (b) a transferee to whom a first home owner grant would be ...
-- payable ... had ... (2)(b) if the transaction is a contract for the purchase of an established home, the transaction would
-- be ... an eligible transaction but for the FHOG Act section 14(5A)." The (2)(a) limb (no consideration) is not encoded.
-- Completion is not required ("is or will be payable"). The WA Duties Act baseline asks this as a fact; this is its answer.
GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a concessional first home owner` IF
        `every applicant meets every criterion` `the application`
    AND `the application`'s `every owner who must apply has applied`
    AND `it is an eligible transaction but for s 14(5A)` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)

@export Am I a concessional first home owner for the transfer duty concession (Duties Act 2008 s 142A, read with this Act)?
GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your purchase and every buyer, as an application for the grant would state them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a concessional first home owner for duty` IF `I am a concessional first home owner` `the application`
